WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:06.000
This lecture shows how to prune tomato plants.

00:06.000 --> 00:14.000
Suckers are the small shoots that grow between the main stem and a leaf.

00:14.000 --> 00:22.000
Remove each sucker when it is shorter than 5 centimeters. Pinch it off with your fingers.

00:22.000 --> 00:30.000
Keep one main stem on each plant, and tie the stem to a string once a week.

00:30.000 --> 00:38.000
Before you cut a larger stem, wipe the blade of the pruner with alcohol.

00:38.000 --> 00:46.000
Remove the leaves below the first group of flowers.

00:46.000 --> 00:52.000
Prune in the morning on a dry day, so that the cuts dry fast.

00:52.000 --> 01:00.000
